    "description": "ADD (AI-Driven Development) — a minimal, state-tracked workflow for building software where the AI writes the code and the human owns direction and verification. Drives every feature through one lean TASK.md: Specify → Scenarios → Contract → Tests → Build → Verify → Observe, with red/green TDD built in. Use this skill whenever working in a repo that has a `.add/` directory, when the user says \"add\", \"start a task\", \"next phase\", \"specify this feature\", \"ADD method\", or \"AI-driven development\", or when scaffolding a new feature and you want spec/tests-first discipline instead of vague-prompt coding. Also use it to resume work across sessions (it reads `.add/state.json` so you never re-read the whole repo).",
